\b \cf0 On top of the raft system, there are several constraints in implementing the ticketing system:
\b0 \
	1. The # of available tickets never go under zero:\
	    The ticket sell write should only be applied to the leader, this indicates if the number of tickets after the write is below zero, then such request should be rejected, else if it\'92s above zero, then write can be proceed and an acknowledgment message should be sent back to the client to confirm that the purchase is done. \
\
	2. The consistent read/write should be as not very frequent to give good performance to the system.\
	Any frontend get the number of tickets by quering(message exchange) its corresponded node. The result is an unstable read, meaning it's the result of applying both committed and uncommited log entries to the state machine of any node.\
\
\
\
\

\b Ticketing System Implementation:\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\b0 \cf0 	Each frontend has a corresponding backend node. It send its unstable read requests and consistent write request to its backend node. The backend node will return its statemachine upon read request, but will reroute the write request to the raft leader. \
\
	The leader, upon receiving the write request, will compare the requested ticket number to the ticket remaining in its statemachine. If there's enough ticket, it will send back an acknowledgement message to the corresponding frontend, else it will send back a failure message notifying there's not enough ticket left. \
\
	\
	To reduce the number of consistent write operation, each client frontend will reserve a certain number of tickets(20) from the backend nodes leader whenever a customer order n tickets exceeding the number of reserved tickets. Any buy request will be process inside the client frontend without consistent write operation unitll is message to the backend node leader is necessary. \
\
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

