\f1\fs26 \cf2 \cb3 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
How does what you've implemented compare to how you might implement similar functionality on top of Bayou? What parts of this would become easier on Bayou (e.g., with custom conflict resolvers), and what might become harder?\cb1 \
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \
If this application is implemented on top of Bayou, as Bayou is a weakly consistent protocol. However, I can still implement the system in a similar way compared to raft. The read access will still be \'93unstable\'94 reads and the values are those returned from any backend server node the frontend communicates.  We can not enforce a consistent write operation as we don\'92t really know how long can we wait until the system reach final consistency. However, this is not much of a problem if we only allow non-primary write operation when ticket number is greater than certain threshold, chosen based on our understanding of how the system behaves in terms of how the actual available tickets changes.  The Bayou protocol would resolve any discrepancies of such write operations between different backend nodes.\
\
When the unstable read is under such threshold, the frontend will communicates with only the primary server, so that any of its write operation will be committed immediately and reduce the chance of letting the number goes below zero.\
\
\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sl300\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\fs26 \cf2 \cb3 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
What additional guarantees does this approach have compared to implementing the functionality on top of CRDTs like the bounded counter CRDT? What advantages does having a single log bring over using CRDTs? (Note: you don't have to read that paper to answer this question.)\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\sl300\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb1 \

\fs24 \cf4 The bounded counter CRDT enforces the number of operations/some threshold on the value before synchronizing the value with other servers.  But Bayou allow some global invariant as constraint which is not possible for CRDT.(1) As for the application we implemented, it enforce consistent write that is not the feature of CRDT, the remaining ticket will never go under zero. \

